From 0f51e13f1f556149250f654fb7c4d49767be2994 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:17:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0189 -- the SDL debug trace defaults OFF
 (DOS_PORT_LOG=1 turns it on)

Consolidates 0188 and 0189 in video/dos/SDL_dosdbg.c.

Every trace line is an fprintf + fflush + fsync on purpose, so a trace
survives a hard reset. On a CF card that is not free, and some callers are in
hot code: DOSVESA_UpdateWindowFramebuffer writes five lines per 100 flushes
from INSIDE the present. Cell FPT1 measured that batch at ~10 ms and, once in
twenty-four, at 227 ms, which was the whole ~250 ms present stall the
campaign had been chasing since Gate 2 opened.

Cell LOGAB, four cells and one binary with the arms set by this environment
variable: with the trace on, both cells stalled ~277 ms at tick 2403 and
dropped 12 and 17 frames; with it off, neither stalled and both dropped 4.

The flag is resolved once and cached, since a getenv per log line would itself
be a cost inside the present. Every diagnostic the trace ever produced is
still reachable with DOS_PORT_LOG=1. A diagnostic that defaults off in a
shipping build is ordinary, and this one is instrumentation the project
added rather than part of the port's function, so no gate figure should mix
a build that carries the instrument with one that does not.

Behaviour change: the trace is OFF by default.

Provenance of this export (2026-09-21): these edits sat uncommitted in the
vendor tree from patch 0123 onward, which is why every gate cell since said
build_dirty=1. They were made under one campaign-wide patch counter shared
with vendor/SDL, and each hunk carries its number in an in-source comment.
Intermediate states were never committed, so this patch is a hunk-level
partition of the final tree by concern, attributed by those comments -- not a
replay of the order the edits were made in, and its intermediate state was not
built on its own. The numbers named below are the ones found in its hunks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/video/dos/SDL_dosdbg.c | 43 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 43 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video/dos/SDL_dosdbg.c b/src/video/dos/SDL_dosdbg.c
index 8d9af0aa5..ecfdfe458 100644
--- a/src/video/dos/SDL_dosdbg.c
+++ b/src/video/dos/SDL_dosdbg.c
@@ -103,8 +103,51 @@ static const char *dos_port_dbg_resolve_path(void)
     return g_dbg_log_path;
 }
 
+// DOS-PORT patch 0188/0189: the trace is OFF unless DOS_PORT_LOG=1.
+//
+// Every line below costs an fprintf + fflush + fsync, deliberately, so a
+// trace survives a hard reset. On a CF card that is not free, and the
+// callers are not all in cold code: DOSVESA_UpdateWindowFramebuffer writes
+// five lines per 100 flushes from INSIDE the present. dosags cell FPT1
+// measured that batch at ~10 ms every time, and once in twenty-four at
+// 227 ms -- which was the entire ~250 ms present stall this campaign had
+// been chasing since Gate 2 opened.
+//
+// DEFAULT FLIPPED TO OFF, 2026-09-20, after LOGAB measured what it costs.
+// DOS_PORT_LOG=1 turns it back on and everything it ever diagnosed is still
+// reachable that way.
+//
+// LOGAB, four cells, one binary, arms by this env var: with the trace on,
+// both cells stalled ~277 ms at tick 2403 and dropped 12 and 17 frames;
+// with it off, neither stalled at all and both dropped 4. Three to four
+// times fewer dropped frames on a 40 Hz target, from removing one disk
+// write from inside the present.
+//
+// A diagnostic that defaults off in a shipping build is ordinary. This one
+// is also, specifically, instrumentation this project added rather than
+// part of the port's function -- the same class as the fixture's own
+// logging, which the operator already ruled on, and for the same reason
+// they ruled: so that no gate figure mixes provenance between a build that
+// carries the instrument and one that does not.
+//
+// Resolved once, on first use, and cached: a getenv per log line would
+// itself be a cost inside the present.
+static int g_dbg_enabled = -1;
+
+static int dos_port_dbg_enabled(void)
+{
+    if (g_dbg_enabled < 0) {
+        const char *e = SDL_getenv("DOS_PORT_LOG");
+        g_dbg_enabled = (e && e[0] == '1' && e[1] == 0) ? 1 : 0;
+    }
+    return g_dbg_enabled;
+}
+
 void dos_port_dbg_open(void)
 {
+    if (!dos_port_dbg_enabled()) {
+        return;
+    }
     if (!g_dbg_log) {
         g_dbg_log = fopen(dos_port_dbg_resolve_path(), "wb");
     }
-- 
